<% content_for :title, "Cookie policy" %>

<div class="content-grid">
  <div class="row mt-4 mt-md-5">
    <article class="col-12 col-md-8 col-offset-md-2">
      <hgroup>
        <h1>Cookie policy</h1>
        <p>Updated on <time datetime="2026-11-10">November 10, 2026</time></p>
      </hgroup>

      <%= render "draft_notice" %>

      <%= render "operator_details" %>

      <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="fs-3 mb-2">Sign-in and security</h2>
        <p>ShakeStir uses a signed session_id cookie to recognize your sign-in session. It is configured as a persistent cookie and is cleared in your browser when you log out. Rails also uses a session cookie for browser session state, such as returning you to a page after signing in and request security.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="fs-3 mb-2">Managing cookies</h2>
        <p>You can clear or block cookies in your browser settings. Blocking the service’s cookies may prevent sign-in and account actions from working. Logging out ends the current sign-in session; deleting your account removes all of its server-side sign-in sessions.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="fs-3 mb-2">Other services</h2>
        <p>Gravatar may receive browser requests for the account avatar fallback. See the <%= link_to "privacy policy", privacy_path %> for details. The current application code does not include advertising or analytics trackers. Hosting integrations and any third-party cookies must be checked in the production deployment before this policy is finalized.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="fs-3 mb-2">Before launch</h2>
        <p>Confirm the deployed cookie names, actual lifetimes and purposes, and review any consent requirements for the regions served. This page describes cookies; it does not implement a consent preference system.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
